				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9ef6bf62-0897-585e-8619-842b3941aa9f")
	)
	(text_box "0456025.ER: 25 A, very fast-acting, 1000 A interrupting at 32 V DC, cold resistance 1.92 mOhm, melting I2t 45 A2s (456\nseries datasheet rev. 04/27/16). Drop at 9.2 A: 18 mV, 0.16 W.\nDEPARTURE: the design asks for 'time-lag'; no surface-mount 25 A time-lag fuse was found. 100 % rating carries 4 h minimum;\n9.2 A average is 37 % of rating; the 21 A peaks are switching ripple drawn from the charger's bulk capacitors, not through\nthis fuse at full height [VERIFY with the charger input filter on 10].\nCoordination: a hard short on VBAT_SYS is ended by the MAX17320 short-circuit comparator (65 A, 192 us); the fuse is the\nbackup for a failed protector (FET short)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 93.694 0)
		(size 140 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "60143688-aba0-510d-98b2-d1258b8cd9e9")
	)
	(text_box "Battery-under-load test: 2 x 0.40 ohm PWR263S in series, Q103, hardware on-time limit (TLV7031 + RC, 124-220 ms)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 201.166 0)
		(size 193.16 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3ed7c459-75bb-5c91-a936-14d59ef1354f")
	)
	(text_box "Load: R102 + R103 = 0.80 ohm (DEPARTURE from 0.82 ohm: 0.82 is not a catalogue value of a part with a published pulse rating; two in series halve the energy per part). At\n8.4 V: 8.4 / 0.809 ohm (incl. FET, fuse, sense, FETs) = 10.4 A, 86 W, 43 W per resistor; 100 ms test = 4.3 J per resistor.\nPulse rating: Bourns PWR263S-35 'Pulse Power Rating' graph reads about 8 J at 0.1 s (graph ends at 0.1 s) -> 4.3 J at 100 ms has 1.9x margin; the worst-case 220 ms\nhardware limit gives 9.5 J per resistor, beyond the graph [UNVERIFIED: VERIFY with Bourns; short-term overload 2 x Pr = 70 W per part is stated for R < 2 ohm, 43 W is\nbelow it]. Design target 25 J single pulse in total = 12.5 J per part: [UNVERIFIED].\nTime limit: BAT_LOAD_EN (100k pull-down R110, contract) is AC-coupled by C108 2.2 uF into R111 118 k (tau = 260 ms). The comparator U102 turns Q103 on while the node is\nabove about half of 3V3_MAIN: on at the rising edge, off when the node decays below the threshold, off at once when BAT_LOAD_EN falls (node steps negative). R116 1 M adds\nhysteresis: threshold 1.73 V while on, 1.57 V while off (at 3.3 V).\nOn-time = tau x ln(21/11) = 0.647 tau = 168 ms nominal; C 2.2 uF X7R x0.765..x1.265 (10 % tolerance, 15 % over temperature) and R 1 % -> tau 197-332 ms; threshold factor\n0.631-0.662 (1 % divider, +/-8 mV offset) -> 124-220 ms. Firmware uses <= 100 ms (design §B1.3). Ratiometric to 3V3_MAIN, so supply tolerance cancels.\nR112 10 k limits the comparator input current when the node goes to -3.3 V at the falling edge: 0.33 mA << 10 mA abs max (TLV7031 SLVSE13J 5.1).\nLimitation (capture notes, doubt 3): repeated rising edges re-trigger the timer; a pin toggled at a high rate can hold the load on for up to about half the time. The\nlimit covers a STUCK-HIGH line, not a toggling one.\nUnpowered: 3V3_MAIN off -> U102 unpowered -> R115 holds the gate low (load off). R11: an open or unpowered BAT_LOAD_EN reads 'load off'.\nQ103 CSD17573Q5B: 30 V, IDM 400 A, RDS(on) 1.45 mOhm max at VGS 4.5 V; at the comparator's ~3.2 V gate drive RDS(on) is only given by the curve [UNVERIFIED value, VGS(th)\n1.1-1.8 V]; even 10 mOhm would dissipate 1 W for 0.2 s."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 207.516 0)
